<title>HONG KONG: HAECO undertakes China maintenance deal.</title>
<headline>HAECO undertakes China maintenance deal.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong Aircraft Engineering Company (HAECO) said in a statement on Monday it has undertaken its first major maintenance contract for Airbus Industrie A320 aircraft from China.</p>
<p>The company completed category &quot;C&quot; checks on a Sichuan Airlines A320 aircraft in March, under a contract covering the airline's entire fleet of three A320s, it said.</p>
<p>It was now working on the second A320, with another plane arriving before end May, it said.</p>
<p>Sichuan Airlines is the first operator of the A320 in China where there are now 30 such aircraft, the statement said.</p>
<p>--HONG KONG NEWSROOM (852) 28436441</p>
</text>
